# secrets
.env
*.key
secrets.*
# The pattern above is meant to catch stray real-secret dumps (secrets.json,
# secrets.txt, etc.) -- but on a case-insensitive filesystem/git config (the
# default on Windows) it ALSO silently matches docs/SECRETS.md, this
# project's actual (non-secret) policy doc, excluding it from git with no
# warning. Caught by manually reviewing `git status` before the first
# commit -- see docs/SECRETS.md itself for why that check matters. Explicit
# exception so this can't happen again:
!docs/SECRETS.md

# Kindle daemon's real config (contains your home LAN IP and any local
# overrides). kindle-daemon/config.example.lua stays tracked as the
# template; the real kindle-daemon/src/config.lua does not.
kindle-daemon/src/config.lua

# Cached Kindle IP from the ops start/stop scripts -- local network state,
# not something to version.
kindle-daemon/ops/.last_kindle_ip.txt

# Claude Code's own local settings -- machine-specific absolute paths and
# permission grants, not something to share/version.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Claude Code's session lock files -- runtime artifacts (session ID, PID,
# start time), not something to version. Previously excluded only via
# .git/info/exclude (local-only, not shared with a fresh clone) -- added
# here too so anyone else who clones this repo gets the same exclusion.
.claude/*.lock

# python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/

# build artifacts
*.o
*.out
build/

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
